/* A call that went through a permission review is worth spotting in a scan
   down the transcript, so its whole line turns amber: glyph, verb, subject,
   and trailing status, not one word of it. Muted well below the warning
   orange, because a review is a fact about the call rather than a failure and
   a transcript where most calls were reviewed should still read as prose.
   These follow the single-line rules because they must win over them at equal
   specificity, and they yield to a failure, which is the louder fact. */
.happy-agent-activity[data-review]:not([data-failed]) .happy-agent-activity__header,
.happy-agent-activity[data-review]:not([data-failed]) .happy-agent-activity__glyph,
.happy-agent-activity[data-review]:not([data-failed]) .happy-agent-activity__verb,
.happy-agent-activity[data-review]:not([data-failed]) .happy-agent-activity__text,
